# Supabase — required for sign-in, sign-up and password reset.
#
# Create a project at https://supabase.com, then Project Settings → API.
# Both values are safe in the browser bundle: the ANON key's privileges are
# whatever Row Level Security grants an anonymous or authenticated user.
#
# NEVER put the service_role key here. It bypasses RLS, and every VITE_* value
# is inlined into the JavaScript shipped to users.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key

# Without these the app still builds and runs: sign-in reports that it is not
# configured, and NOTHING is gated, so a misconfigured deploy stays usable
# rather than locking everyone out behind a form that cannot work.

# ── Calculation API ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The steel solvers run server-side as Vercel EDGE FUNCTIONS in `api/steel/`,
# served from this same deployment at /api/steel/*. That is the default and it
# needs NO variable here — leave VITE_API_URL unset.
#
# Set it only for a SPLIT SETUP: the endpoints on another host, or `vercel dev`
# on a second port while Vite serves the SPA. No trailing slash.
# VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# The endpoints themselves need Supabase to check the caller's token. They
# accept either spelling, so the two VITE_ variables above already satisfy
# them — set the unprefixed pair only if you want the server values to differ:
#   SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# See api/README.md. No service-role key is needed there.

# ── The guest trial gate ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GUEST_TRIAL_SALT is what makes the five-runs-per-calculator gate WORK. It
# salts the digest the endpoint counts a guest by; without it no subject can
# be derived, the gate allows everything, and every guest has an unlimited
# allowance. It fails open on purpose — a counter that is down must not take
# the calculators down — but it logs on every request and sets
# `x-calc-quota: degraded; no-salt` on the response, so that state is visible
# rather than silently generous.
#
# NOT a VITE_ variable, and it must never reach the browser: an unsalted
# SHA-256 of an IPv4 address is reversible in minutes, so publishing the salt
# would turn the trial table into a log of who visited from where.
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Use the SAME value as the guest-quota Edge Function's GUEST_TRIAL_SALT. The
# browser's counter and the endpoint's key the same rows, and they only derive
# the same subject under the same salt — differing salts give one visitor two
# separate allowances.
# GUEST_TRIAL_SALT=
#
# Runs per calculator before a guest is asked to sign up. Defaults to 5, which
# is what the pricing page promises and what the UI counts down from.
# GUEST_TRIAL_LIMIT=5

# ── Paddle checkout ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Set all six and the pricing page grows working Choose-plan buttons. Leave any
# of them unset and checkout stays off, the page says paid plans are not open
# yet, and no card details are collected anywhere. Half-configured is treated
# as OFF, never as partly on — see src/lib/billing/paddleConfig.ts.
#
# The CLIENT TOKEN is public by design: it can open a checkout and read prices,
# nothing more, and it is meant to ship in the bundle. Paddle > Developer tools
# > Authentication. The API KEY (`pdl_…`) can move money and must NEVER appear
# in a VITE_ variable — it belongs only in the seed script's shell and in
# Supabase secrets.
#
# THE TOKEN AND THE ENVIRONMENT MUST AGREE. A `test_` token goes with sandbox
# and a `live_` token with production; the app refuses to boot checkout on a
# mismatch rather than risk charging a real card during a test.
# VITE_PADDLE_CLIENT_TOKEN=test_your-sandbox-client-token
# VITE_PADDLE_ENV=sandbox
#
# Price ids from `npx tsx ../scripts/seed-paddle-catalog.ts`, which prints
# these four lines ready to paste. They are environment-scoped — a sandbox
# `pri_…` does not exist in production, so both sets change together.
# VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_PRO_MONTHLY=pri_...
# VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_PRO_ANNUAL=pri_...
# VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_MAX_MONTHLY=pri_...
# VITE_PADDLE_PRICE_MAX_ANNUAL=pri_...
#
# The other half of checkout is the webhook that actually grants the plan —
# supabase/functions/billing-webhook, configured with BILLING_PROVIDER=paddle,
# BILLING_WEBHOOK_SECRET and BILLING_PRICE_MAP. Without it, payments succeed
# and nobody's plan changes. See docs/Billing.md.
